{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791817954,"nonce":"kQgRm7zeHKDUNIGKftbQdwo0J/0=","title":"Array.remove matches closures with different captured values","message":"Local release target/release/ash --preset application removes the first callback when asked to remove a distinct second closure from the same function. This breaks AshUI callback cleanup: hiding one editor panel removes another panel's layout observer, leaving a stale callback registered.\n\nReproducer in sibling ChimpMonk: repro/ash_closure_remove/Repro.hx.\nFrom the ChimpMonk workspace:\n  haxe -cp repro/ash_closure_remove -main Repro -hl /tmp/ash-closure-remove.hl\n  ../ash/target/release/ash --preset application /tmp/ash-closure-remove.hl\n\nExpected: Remaining callback: 1.\nActual: Remaining callback: 2, followed by assertion failure.\nHaxe --interp prints 1 and passes. Reflect.compareMethods(first,second) returns false on both. Captured instance methods show the same Array.remove behavior. Explicitly scan with Reflect.compareMethods and splice the matched index preserves the correct callback.\n\nAsh source HEAD at investigation: eed0d01324e859e594fca6eb7050ebdbc8671c54. This was run against the existing local release binary; no Ash rebuild or edits were made. Other presets have not been tested. Investigate closure comparison in the generic array lookup/removal path.","files":null}]}